Notebook Cell 4: Einselection & Environmental Decoherence (Pointer States)

To test the physics and qualia-stabilization claim (why discrete, classical \
descriptions emerge from continuous high-frequency fields), this notebook \
models a Lindblad-style master equation showing how non-diagonal phase \
correlations decay while pointer states diagonalize.

```mathematica
(* ========================================================= *)
(* 4. EINSELECTION DYNAMICS & POINTER STATE STABILIZATION     *)
(* ========================================================= *)

ClearAll[LindbladDecoherence];

(* 2-level open quantum system coupled to phase noise *)
LindbladDecoherence[gamma_Real, tMax_Real] := Module[{sigmaZ, rho0, eqns, sol},
  sigmaZ = PauliMatrix[3];
  
  (* Pure superposition initial state: (|0> + |1>)/Sqrt[2] *)
  rho0 = {{1/2, 1/2}, {1/2, 1/2}};
  
  (* Analytic solution for purely dephasing Lindblad channel:
     d\[Rho]/dt = -gamma/2 [\[Sigma]z, [\[Sigma]z, \[Rho]]] *)
  Plot[
    {
      1/2,                        (* Diagonal element \[Rho]_00 (Probability) \
*)
      (1/2) * Exp[-2 * gamma * t] (* Off-diagonal |\[Rho]_01| (Quantum \
Coherence) *)
    },
    {t, 0, tMax},
    PlotLegends -> {\"Pointer State Pop (p_0)\", \"Off-Diagonal Phase \
Coherence (|rho_01|)\"},
    AxesLabel -> {\"Interaction Time (t)\", \"State Amplitude\"},
    PlotStyle -> {Thick, Dashed},
    PlotLabel -> \"Einselection: Environmental Phase Decoherence Selecting \
Classical Observable\"
  ]
];

LindbladDecoherence[0.5, 5.0]
```

