documentation snippets using semantic search.\nArguments\n\tquery - A natural \
language question or description of what you're trying to achieve\n\nWeb \
Fetcher (/web_fetch)\nFetch plain text or image links from a URL.\nArguments\n\
\turl - The URL\n\tformat - The type of content to retrieve (\"Plaintext\" or \
\"ImageLinks\")\n\nWeb Image Searcher (/img_search)\nSearch the web for \
images.\nArguments\n\tquery - Search query text\n\nWeb Searcher (/web_search)\
\nSearch the web.\nArguments\n\tquery - Search query text\n\nWolfram|Alpha \
(/wa)\nUse natural language queries with Wolfram|Alpha to get up-to-date \
computational results about entities in chemistry, physics, geography, \
history, art, astronomy, and more.\nIMPORTANT: If you need the results of \
multiple queries, it's important that you combine them into a single tool \
