model object**\n   - inputs\n   - states\n   - outputs\n   - update law\n   - \
sampling period if discrete\n\n10. **pipeline object**\n   - \\(L_0 \\to L_1 \
\\to L_2\\) composition\n   - symbolic and numerical branches\n\n---\n\n# 10. \
Potential algorithms, grouped by purpose\n\nHere is a cleaner \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]master list\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\n## Q. Master \
algorithm inventory\n\n### Derivation\n- variational derivation\n- \
constrained variation\n- symbolic elimination\n- dimensional balancing\n- \
symmetry detection\n\n### Solution\n- exact ODE/PDE solving\n- separable \
ansatz solving\n- transform methods\n- fixed-point methods\n- continuation \
methods\n- arbitrary-precision nonlinear solving\n\n### Stability\n- \
linearization\n- eigenanalysis\n- Lyapunov construction\n- energy estimates\n\
- perturbation propagation\n- pseudospectral analysis\n\n### \
Geometry/topology\n- compactification\n- defect detection\n- homotopy \
classification\n- curvature extraction\n- topological equivalence testing\n\n\
### Information/computation\n- entropy minimization\n- complexity estimation\n\
- information flow inference\n- compression-based structure discovery\n- \
residual-guided refinement\n\n### Measurement\n- basis optimization\n- \
projection/decoherence\n- observable synthesis\n- inverse measurement \
reconstruction\n- repeated-observation updating\n\n### Systems/controls\n- \
state-space construction\n- transfer operator construction\n- discrete I/O \
iteration\n- stability margins\n- controllability/observability analogs\n\n\
### Model selection\n- compare candidate density definitions\n- compare \
function spaces\n- compare topologies\n- compare measurement kernels\n- rank \
by residual/stability/interpretablity\n\n---\n\n# 11. Functional tests \
specifically for \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]spacetime density\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\n\nIf your main target is density of spacetime, then \
these are the first essential tests.\n\n## R. Density-specific test suite\n\n\
1. **positivity test**\n   - is the proposed density nonnegative?\n\n2. \
**integrability test**\n   - does total density converge on the domain?\n\n3. \
**scale invariance test**\n   - does density preserve OPF scale logic?\n\n4. \
**boundary behavior test**\n   - what happens at \\(0\\) and \\(\\infty\\)?\n\
\n5. **resolution covariance test**\n   - how does density transform under \
\\(R \\mapsto \\tilde R\\)?\n\n6. **measurement consistency test**\n   - does \
measured density agree with latent density?\n\n7. **spectral consistency \
test**\n   - do density peaks correspond to stable modes?\n\n8. **stability \
generation test**\n   - does higher density stabilize or destabilize \
solutions?\n\n9. **emergent geometry test**\n   - can density induce \
effective curvature/metric?\n\n10. **inverse recoverability test**\n   - can \
density be inferred from observables?\n\n11. **topological sensitivity test**\
\n   - does density depend on substrate topology?\n\n12. **computational \
tractability test**\n   - can it be evaluated/refined effectively?\n\n---\n\n\
# 12. A full mathematical structure for your logic\n\nHere is the concise \
formal scaffold I\[CloseCurlyQuote]d recommend.\n\n## S. OPF mathematical \
skeleton\n\n### S1. Substrate\nLet\n$$\n\
\\mathcal{S}_0=(X,\\tau,\\beta,\\sigma)\n$$\nwhere:\n- \\(X\\) is a \
sphere-like topological substrate,\n- \\(\\tau\\) is topology,\n- \
\\(\\beta=\\{0,\\infty\\}\\) is boundary duality,\n- \\(\\sigma\\) is \
symmetry structure.\n\n### S2. Field layer\nDefine fields\n$$\n\\rho,\\chi,R \
: X \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\nwith admissibility:\n$$\n\\rho \\ge 0,\\quad \\chi \
> 0,\\quad R>0\n$$\n\nDefine\n$$\n\\Psi = \\Psi[\\rho,\\chi,R]\n$$\n\n### S3. \
Action\n$$\nS[\\rho,\\chi,R] = \\int_X \
\\mathcal{L}(\\rho,\\chi,R,\\nabla\\rho,\\nabla\\chi,\\nabla R,\\dots)\\, \
d\\mu\n$$\n\nstart with\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}_0=\\rho\\log\\chi+\\chi R^2\n$$\n\n\
then extend if needed.\n\n### S4. Field equations\nCompute\n$$\n\
\\frac{\\delta S}{\\delta \\rho}=0,\\qquad\n\\frac{\\delta S}{\\delta \
\\chi}=0,\\qquad\n\\frac{\\delta S}{\\delta R}=0\n$$\n\npossibly with \
constraints.\n\n### S5. Linearization\nAt a background solution \
\\((\\rho_0,\\chi_0,R_0)\\), write\n$$\n\\rho=\\rho_0+\\epsilon \
\\hat\\rho,\\quad\n\\chi=\\chi_0+\\epsilon \\hat\\chi,\\quad\nR=R_0+\\epsilon \
\\hat R\n$$\nand derive the linear operator\n$$\n\\mathcal{J}\n\
\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\hat\\rho\\\\\\hat\\chi\\\\\\hat R\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\
=\\lambda\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\hat\\rho\\\\\\hat\\chi\\\\\\hat R\n\
\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n### S6. Stable resonances\nExtract\n$$\n\\{\\lambda : \
\\Re(\\lambda)=0,\\ \\Im(\\lambda)>0\\}\n$$\n\n### S7. Measurement map\n\
Define\n$$\n\\mathcal{M} : \\Psi \\mapsto \\mathcal{O}\n$$\nby\n$$\n\
\\mathcal{O}=\\int \\Psi\\, d\\mu_{\\text{eig}}\n$$\n\n### S8. Persistent \
reality layer\nMeasured states \\(u\\) satisfy\n$$\n\\partial_t u+\\Gamma u=0\
\n$$\nor generalized maintenance equations.\n\n### S9. Composition\nThe full \
system is\n$$\n\\mathfrak{P}=\\mathcal{M}\\circ \\mathcal{E}\\circ \
\\mathcal{T}\n$$\nwhere:\n- \\(\\mathcal{T}\\): topology-to-field \
admissibility map\n- \\(\\mathcal{E}\\): field evolution/solution map\n- \
\\(\\mathcal{M}\\): measurement map\n\nThat gives you a clean compositional \
ontology.\n\n---\n\n# 13. What to dissect first\n\nTo avoid drowning in \
possibilities, I recommend this order:\n\n## Phase 1: Minimal formal model\n\
1. define \\(X\\), \\(d\\mu\\), and admissibility conditions\n2. formalize \
\\(\\mathcal{L}_0=\\rho\\log\\chi+\\chi R^2\\)\n3. derive Euler equations\n4. \
identify degeneracies\n\n## Phase 2: Density definitions\n5. compare \
\\(D_1\\) through \\(D_{10}\\)\n6. decide what \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]spacetime density\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] means in OPF\
\n\n## Phase 3: Stability machinery\n7. linearize\n8. extract spectral modes\n\
9. define stable resonance criteria\n\n## Phase 4: Measurement layer\n10. \
define eigenbasis and measurement kernel\n11. encode latent-to-observable map\
\n\n## Phase 5: Input/output conversion\n12. represent each stage as a \
state-space or operator I/O system\n\n---\n\n# 14. Best possible next \
deliverables\n\nI can do any of these next:\n\n1. **Build a master taxonomy \
table**  \n   A large structured table of every object/test/algorithm/I/O \
